{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1421796-bogatyrs-of-russia","id":1421796,"title":"Bogatyrs of Russia?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-04T07:40:11-08:00","id":1421796,"title":"Bogatyrs of Russia?","content":"So I\u2019m talking about Bogatyrs, so-called \u201cthe Three Knights\u201d in Russian folklore of reality <br /> <br /> In CWoD, it is rumored that they sent Baba Yaga into torpor (!), but all suffered tragic death at last. Vampires, Mage and Werewolves claim them as their own. And interesting enough, in Nights of Prophecy the house of Yaga has painting of them which will change by time (?!). I think it has much to exploit, but canon stuff is few? What\u2019s your opinion about them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T10:35:37-08:00","id":1421813,"title":"","content":"Didn't Clanbook Tzimisce have them as some sort of strange creatures that washed up in the Carpathians after the deluge and served the Eldest? Maybe they're something completely different than the standard Vamp/Mage/Werewolf. Or maybe there's multiple supernaturals claiming the name as their own and the answer is all of the above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T11:03:30-08:00","id":1421818,"title":"","content":"I personally hold that most of the great mythic or legendary heroes of humanity, including the Bogatyr, are probably a kind of Mage from a &quot;lost&quot; heroic Tradition or Craft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T16:42:53-08:00","id":1421872,"title":"","content":"It depends. There's a bunch of them, including female Polianitsa. A few are actual historical people. Then you have ones like the giant Svyatogor who is clearly not. (He's one I'd say is probably one of the True Fey.) Others may be Garou (Silver Fangs, Fenrir, Black Furies, Shadow Lords) or other Fera (Gurahl, Corax), Mages of various styles (especially Old Faith/Verbena, Spirit Talkers/Dreamspeakers, and Messianic Voices/Celestial Chorus), vampires, and True Faith empowered holy warriors, among things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T17:18:38-08:00","id":1421880,"title":"","content":"The first word on them for the WoD was in Rage Across Russia, which presented them as being Garou and Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T18:55:26-08:00","id":1421903,"title":"","content":"Garou and Mages...? That's the deadliest combo in the entire series, lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T19:30:24-08:00","id":1421914,"title":"","content":"I think that like the knights of the Round Table, the Bogatyrs may come from diverse supernatural backgrounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}